  "question": {
    "text": "A block is kept on a smooth inclined plane of the angle of inclination&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>°</mo></math> that moves with a constant acceleration so that the block does not slide relative to the inclined plane. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> be the contact force between the block and the plane. Now the inclined plane stops and let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> be the contact force between the two in this case. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is",
